# `libxslt/` is a 2,245-file git clone with its OWN `.git`, checked out as a
# dependency. It is a checkout, not source, and one `git add -A` from committing
# an entire dependency history. This rule has now been lost twice to unrelated
# .gitignore rewrites (first in 2c3a58eb), so it is short and stands alone.
libxslt/

# `validation/m55/profile/user-data/` is a CAPTURED BROWSER PROFILE, not a
# fixture and not evidence: 230 files, 33 MB, produced by an m55 profiling run of
# the agent host. It contains `Cookies` (+ journal), `machineid`, `Local State`,
# `Preferences`, `Trust Tokens`, `SharedStorage`, `Network Persistent State`,
# `TransportSecurity`, `Crashpad`, GPU/CDAWN caches, `chatSessions` and
# `workspaceStorage`.
#
# It is untracked, and it must STAY untracked: committing it would publish browser
# session material and a stable machine identifier to a public repository, and no
# later `git rm` makes that reversible. Found during the pre-push review, when a
# `git add -A` staged all 230 of them in one go. Nothing of it was ever in HEAD
# or in any commit on origin/main, so nothing needs undoing.
#
# The rule is scoped to the CAPTURED profile, not to `validation/m55/`, so the
# m55 lane's own reports and assertions under that tree remain committable.
validation/m55/profile/
# ...including `extensions/backbencher.bb-lsp-vscode-0.1.0/`, which is a CAPTURED
# COPY of this repo's own extension. `ide/vscode/` is tracked and is the real
# source; the copy under the profile differs from it in `package.json`, so if that
# difference was deliberate it belongs committed in `ide/vscode/`, where a reader
# will look — not as a build artefact inside a profiling capture. Flagged for the
# m55 lane rather than silently resolved here.
